course: dictionary
lesson: 6166
title: Small words: mini
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mini means very small, or smaller than usual. When you see it in a text, look at the words around it. «The shop sold mini pizzas for one pound each.» The word pizzas tells you what is being described, and mini tells you each pizza is small. Ask yourself: what is small here?
explain: Mini also works as the start of other words, and it always adds the idea of small. «We went on a bug hunt and found minibeasts under the logs.» A minibeast is a small creature, like a woodlouse or a beetle. Once you know mini means small, you can often work out the new word without looking it up.
explain: Sometimes mini is a name, not a description. «A Mini is a small British car.» Look for a capital letter and the words around it. Here the clue is car: a Mini is a kind of car, not a small thing in general.
fact: Mini means very small, or smaller than usual.
fact: As the start of a word, mini- means "small": minibus, minibeast, miniskirt and mini-golf all have this meaning.
fact: «Mini» can also be a short name for a small British car, called a Mini, with a capital M.
fact: In school you may hear «mini whiteboards», «a mini quiz» or «a mini project»; in each one, mini tells you the thing is small.
fact: Informal: a mini is a short skirt, also called a miniskirt.
exercise: «The shop sold mini pizzas for one pound each.» What does mini mean here? | *Very small | Very late | Very loud | Very hot
exercise: «We went on a bug hunt and found minibeasts under the logs.» What is a minibeast? | A tiny rocket | A type of pizza | *A small creature, like a woodlouse or a beetle | A big animal like a lion
exercise: Mini is a start of a word that means small. Which word means a small bus? | *Minibus | Bustle | Busy | Doubledecker
test: «A log pile is a mini habitat that shelters many minibeasts.» What does mini tell you about the habitat? | It means a home for cars | *It means a small home | It means a wet home | It means a huge home
test: Kieran's friend calls him «mini-me». What does it mean? | A new haircut | A tiny robot | *A small copy of someone else | A football team
exam: «A Mini is a small British car.» What is a Mini? | *A small British car | A bright blue sweet | A dinosaur | A type of big bus
